      "title": "Deployment Options",
      "lectureOrder": 111,
      "videoOrder": 104,
      "sourceHash": "ddf201a4076d960382dadaea6dc3ba5a387565a105f2f645c326b3f4e55cc356",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "When it comes to deploying Remix apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 6.696,
          "en": "you have different choices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.696,
          "end": 11.696,
          "en": "To be precise, when you create a Remix application with npx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.97,
          "end": 14.61,
          "en": "create Remix at latest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 19.08,
          "en": "you don't just get asked for the name of your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.08,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "but you also get asked where you want to deploy it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "Now the list of options here might change over time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 29.253,
          "en": "but in general, Remix supports different deployment targets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "Now, you can use the Remix app server and deploy your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 38.67,
          "en": "on any hosting machine that supports node JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.67,
          "end": 42.48,
          "en": "But you can also choose more specific deployment provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.48,
          "end": 45.87,
          "en": "which often makes deployment a bit easier than",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 50.073,
          "en": "if you run your own node JS server, for example, Netlify.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 52.56,
          "en": "And if you wanna deploy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.56,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "to such a target to Netlify for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "you should create a project where you make that choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 61.65,
          "en": "And that's exactly what I'm doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.65,
          "end": 64.8,
          "en": "I'm creating a new project where I chose Netlify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.8,
          "end": 66.25,
          "en": "as the deployment target",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.29,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "and then add your code to that project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 73.05,
          "en": "If you already have a Remix project where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.05,
          "end": 76.65,
          "en": "you chose a different deployment target, as it's the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.65,
          "end": 80.28,
          "en": "for us here, you can simply copy over your app folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 83.58,
          "en": "your public folder, in our case, the prisma folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.58,
          "end": 86.61,
          "en": "and also our dependencies, and you're good to go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.61,
          "end": 88.24,
          "en": "So you can copy that over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "and then use that provider in that project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "And we'll do that in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "Now, Remix supports deployment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "to different platforms through a feature called adapters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 103.05,
          "en": "And as mentioned, we'll probably see more possible targets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.05,
          "end": 106.41,
          "en": "over time, and you can also build your own adapter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.41,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "which of course is a bit more advanced, but you can look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "into this adapter or configuration to learn more about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 117.18,
          "en": "Here we're now going to deploy this application to Netlify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.18,
          "end": 120.993,
          "en": "so that we see one example deployment process in action.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
